      "final_answer": "Because the bag is marked final\u2011sale it can\u2019t be returned or exchanged for a change of mind, but that restriction does not apply if the item is damaged, defective, or incorrect. \u202fAccording to the Damaged or Wrong Items Policy, final\u2011sale items that arrive broken still qualify for review and a possible replacement or refund (04\u2011damaged\u2011or\u2011wrong\u2011items.md\u202f\u2014\u202fFinal\u2011sale items).\u202fThe policy also says the customer must report the issue within 7\u202fcalendar days of delivery (04\u2011damaged\u2011or\u2011wrong\u2011items.md\u202f\u2014\u202fReporting window), and that a return\u2011shipping fee is waived when the item arrived damaged (04\u2011damaged\u2011or\u2011wrong\u2011items.md\u202f\u2014\u202fAvailable resolutions).\n\nIn addition, Aster &\u202fRow\u2019s limited warranty for bags lasts 2\u202fyears from the purchase date and covers manufacturing defects such as a faulty zipper (07\u2011warranty.md\u202f\u2014\u202fWhat is covered). \u202fA broken zipper that is a manufacturing defect would therefore be covered under that warranty as well.\n\n**What to do next**\n\n1.\u202fGather the order ID, clear photos of the damaged zipper and the packaging, and any proof of purchase.\n2.\u202fContact our support team (via chat, email, or phone) and let them know the item arrived damaged.\u202fProvide the order ID and photos.\n3.\u202fThe support specialist will review the claim and, if approved, will arrange a replacement or a refund (the shipping fee is waived for damaged items) or process a warranty claim if the product is still within the 2\u2011year period.\n\nYou\u2019re definitely not out of luck\u2014this defect is covered by the damaged\u2011",
